  "findings": [
    "Bounded support: fresh leading/interior/trailing blanks, mixed size23/8/17 lines, root versus children, deeper left/right nodes, escaped-backslash parity and raw URL content all pass. WBSDiagram.addIdea calls Display.getWithNewlines; Rust caches one content/height/baseline projection and uses it for measure and emit_box. The raw model labels retain their escapes.",
    "Whole-output counterexample s_display_commands has identical 140x191 canvas and line coordinates, but Java emits q and r as separate atoms around empty size/color commands while Rust emits qr. s_display_escapes also fails due to the retained backslash before tilde. The Display line split is supported; acceptance is rejected because the integrated text component still fails valid held-outs. These are shared-text dependencies, not evidence that the new line projection itself is wrong.",
    "display_forced_alignment is excluded from the verdict exactly as instructed: Java splits Crown/East/West and Branch/Needle using r/l and aligns them, Rust preserves literal backslash-r/backslash-l. Both before and after fail; this is recorded without counting it against the maker.",
    "display_raw_math includes a malformed latex command and the runner lacks Batik. Even syntactically valid s_display_latex_valid (nabla/nu) hits the missing Batik fallback. These three math-related reference outputs across the review are preserved as nonpositive environment residue. Historical golden environment equivalence is unproved."
  ],
